WEBVTT

00:00.780 --> 00:01.970
Holy crap!

00:02.970 --> 00:04.130
It's marbled beef!

00:04.930 --> 00:07.890
That's about 125 dollars worth right there.

00:07.890 --> 00:09.810
125 dollars?

00:09.810 --> 00:11.640
That's so expensive!

00:11.640 --> 00:13.240
What's going on, Master Vamp?

00:13.240 --> 00:14.950
Why the high quality beef?

00:14.950 --> 00:16.810
Did Red die or something?

00:16.810 --> 00:18.180
Nope.

00:18.180 --> 00:22.700
Don't you ever get the urge to enjoy the best of the best from time to time?

00:22.700 --> 00:25.730
I want us to have the best sukiyaki we've ever had today!

00:26.860 --> 00:29.240
You're totally max quality, Master Vamp.

00:29.240 --> 00:31.890
I'm so glad I've lived this long.

00:32.390 --> 00:33.940
I bought us all-organic vegetables,

00:33.940 --> 00:35.440
S-grade iodized eggs,

00:35.440 --> 00:38.040
and to top it off, I prepared the broth fresh at home using bonito and kombu extracts!

00:38.540 --> 00:40.340
A-Awesome...

00:41.340 --> 00:42.880
I'm getting all nervous for some reason.

00:42.880 --> 00:44.920
Dump the broth in already!

00:44.920 --> 00:47.290
Meat, meat, meat!

00:47.290 --> 00:48.870
Hold on to your pants, here.

00:48.870 --> 00:51.430
First we're going to enjoy the meat Kansai style

00:51.430 --> 00:53.180
by seasoning the broth with soy sauce and sugar,

00:53.180 --> 00:54.710
then we'll finish off Kanto style,

00:54.710 --> 00:57.090
by boiling the homemade broth with the rest of the vegetables.

00:57.090 --> 00:59.140
I'm a Matsuzaka beef virgin.

01:00.140 --> 01:04.420
I think in order for us to actually think about conquering the world,

01:04.420 --> 01:06.010
we should at least be able to know what's real.

01:06.910 --> 01:08.330
Let's dig in!

01:08.930 --> 01:10.350
Okay!

01:08.930 --> 01:10.350
Matsuzaka!

01:11.200 --> 01:12.920
Looks like I came just in time!

01:12.920 --> 01:14.120
You guys made sukiyaki?

01:20.290 --> 01:21.950
Are you serious?

01:21.950 --> 01:24.210
This meat looks amazing!

01:24.210 --> 01:26.040
Are you guys celebrating something?

01:26.040 --> 01:28.800
Did you guys come up with a good plan to take me down or what?

01:29.200 --> 01:30.640
But still,

01:30.640 --> 01:34.540
don't you guys think sukiyaki is the best way to enjoy beef?

01:34.540 --> 01:36.350
Beef-bowl restaurants can testify to this,

01:36.350 --> 01:39.620
but there's something about beef and sweet-spicy seasoning that go so well together.

01:40.620 --> 01:42.400
The hot plate's warm already.

01:42.400 --> 01:45.410
Come on, dump the broth in already.

01:45.410 --> 01:47.760
Ow...

01:49.750 --> 01:51.120
What's wrong with you?

01:51.120 --> 01:52.900
You should be used to me beating you up by now.

01:52.900 --> 01:55.260
That actually hurts pretty bad.

01:55.660 --> 01:58.220
You're getting dust all over the meat.

02:02.170 --> 02:03.790
What's wrong with you guys?

02:11.090 --> 02:12.740
I get it now.

02:12.740 --> 02:16.090
So I'm the unwanted guest, is that it?

02:16.090 --> 02:17.600
Well, not really...

02:17.600 --> 02:20.290
Fine, I get it.

02:20.290 --> 02:22.720
I can tell when I'm not wanted.

02:29.760 --> 02:31.860
Should we not have done that?

02:31.860 --> 02:33.650
No, that was totally fine.

02:33.650 --> 02:37.050
We <i>are </i> an evil organization after all.

02:37.050 --> 02:38.540
I-I guess.

02:38.540 --> 02:41.690
But haven't we been spoiling Red a little, lately?

02:41.690 --> 02:43.970
It's as if he thinks we're <i>supposed </i> to feed him, or something.

02:43.970 --> 02:47.170
Yeah, it's not like he's paying us for the food either.

02:47.170 --> 02:48.720
You do have a point, but...

02:48.720 --> 02:51.820
This should serve as a good lesson for him.

02:51.820 --> 02:53.410
Y-Yeah, you're right.

02:53.410 --> 02:54.270
All right then.

02:54.270 --> 02:56.250
Shall we forget about what happened and dig in?

02:57.050 --> 02:58.620
Agreed!

02:57.050 --> 02:58.620
Matsuzaka!

03:02.900 --> 03:05.090
It's time for the sun to set, Sunred.

03:05.590 --> 03:08.080
Fall into a night of despair!

03:08.080 --> 03:10.700
Twin Death Attack!

03:14.090 --> 03:15.710
Are you guys all right?

03:15.710 --> 03:17.920
Don't worry, I'll have them sit up straight right away, Mr. Red.

03:23.340 --> 03:24.400
What's wrong?

03:24.400 --> 03:25.970
Ow...

03:26.410 --> 03:27.810
He's mad.

03:28.790 --> 03:30.750
Mr. Red's mad at us.

03:31.850 --> 03:32.910
How can you tell?

03:32.910 --> 03:35.020
It ended way too quickly!

03:35.020 --> 03:36.290
Too quickly?

03:36.290 --> 03:38.310
But he normally beats us in one blow—

03:38.310 --> 03:43.110
Normally he tends to lecture us or mock us after he beats us, doesn't he?

03:43.110 --> 03:44.480
Even today I thought he'd mock us

03:44.480 --> 03:47.830
and say that all that good meat was wasted on us or something,

03:47.830 --> 03:49.730
but he went back without saying a word!

03:51.320 --> 03:53.870
Maybe he had something important he had to do?

03:53.870 --> 03:56.880
Mr. Red couldn't possibly have anything important to do!

03:57.480 --> 03:59.230
He's mad at us.

03:59.230 --> 04:02.750
He's mad because we didn't let him have any sukiyaki yesterday.

04:02.750 --> 04:04.460
But why?

04:04.460 --> 04:06.360
He's got no reason to be angry!

04:08.350 --> 04:10.070
Hello, Kayoko?

04:10.070 --> 04:11.080
It's me.

04:11.080 --> 04:14.580
Oh yes, I forgot to thank you for that.

04:15.130 --> 04:17.890
You're so good at it, you know.

04:17.890 --> 04:19.530
Yeah. Uh-huh.

04:19.530 --> 04:20.780
Actually...

04:22.090 --> 04:25.400
Nope, he doesn't want to talk to us.

04:25.400 --> 04:27.000
What are we going to do about the next fight?

04:27.000 --> 04:31.640
And here I was, thinking that we'd built up a friendly adversarial relationship.

04:31.640 --> 04:33.230
Should we just commit some random act of terror

04:33.230 --> 04:34.670
if we can't get him to come fight us next time?

04:34.670 --> 04:36.440
He'll just flat out ignore it!

04:36.440 --> 04:37.970
We can't underestimate this guy.

04:39.430 --> 04:42.530
I'd rather have him yelling at us than this.

04:42.530 --> 04:44.710
It's like a cold war, isn't it?

04:44.710 --> 04:46.430
We have to do something.

04:49.400 --> 04:50.120
Who is it?

04:54.720 --> 04:56.220
Why the hell are you punks here?

04:56.220 --> 04:58.530
You haven't had dinner yet, right, Mr. Red?

04:58.530 --> 05:00.590
Eating casseroles is the best thing about winter, you know.

05:00.590 --> 05:03.360
Kayoko, Kayoko!

05:03.360 --> 05:03.970
Why you—

05:03.970 --> 05:05.170
Let's have a casserole party!

05:05.170 --> 05:06.510
Oh, hi Vamp!

05:06.510 --> 05:09.250
You cheap bastard, quit dragging Kayoko to your side!

05:13.920 --> 05:15.850
This doesn't smell at all!

05:15.850 --> 05:16.900
Right?

05:16.900 --> 05:19.580
You can't get this kind of flavor unless you cook the fish straight out of the water.

05:19.580 --> 05:22.060
That angler fish was caught just moments ago!

05:22.060 --> 05:24.990
Hammer Heads went all the way to Hirakata in Ibaraki

05:24.990 --> 05:27.850
just to catch that angler fish with his bare hands!

05:27.850 --> 05:29.560
I should tell you, he's really good at swimming.

05:29.860 --> 05:32.170
Well no shit, he's a shark for cryin' out loud.

05:32.170 --> 05:37.100
They say that the South has fugu, but we up North have angler fish.

05:37.100 --> 05:38.410
How do you like it, Mr. Red?

05:38.410 --> 05:39.950
Isn't it delicious?

05:39.950 --> 05:41.520
Not really.

05:41.520 --> 05:44.520
Angler fish is rich in collagen, you know.

05:44.520 --> 05:48.170
Your skin will be so nice and plump tomorrow morning!

05:48.170 --> 05:50.220
It tastes so good when we all eat together.

05:50.220 --> 05:51.430
Isn't it?

05:51.430 --> 05:52.160
It's so good!

05:52.160 --> 05:53.120
Nice and plump!

05:53.120 --> 05:56.160
Why the hell did he bring <i>these </i> guys along?

05:57.590 --> 05:59.330
Are you even listening?

05:59.330 --> 06:01.350
How many times do I have to tell you punks?

06:01.350 --> 06:04.720
Do you guys even have brains?

06:04.720 --> 06:06.950
Even household insects could do better than you guys.

06:06.950 --> 06:08.220
Take a good look at yourselves, for cryin' out loud—

06:08.220 --> 06:09.970
This is how it should be.

06:09.970 --> 06:10.290
Yeah.

06:10.290 --> 06:11.850
Who said you could talk while I'm talking?

06:11.850 --> 06:13.450
You're right, we're sorry!

06:13.450 --> 06:14.940
Astro Fighter Sunred.

06:14.940 --> 06:17.540
This is the story of the conflict between good and evil

06:17.540 --> 06:19.690
that takes place in the city of Kawasaki.

07:59.520 --> 08:02.300
Oh no, the "Exciting Sexy Summer Experience" booklet's

08:02.300 --> 08:04.560
been opened by something sharp!

08:13.490 --> 08:15.210
Look, it's Master Vamp!

08:15.210 --> 08:16.920
Gotcha! <i>Men </i>!

08:21.250 --> 08:22.670
Y-You okay?

08:22.670 --> 08:23.660
That's one point for me.

08:23.960 --> 08:26.030
Ow...

08:25.260 --> 08:26.030
Aw, poor baby.

08:26.030 --> 08:28.290
That was a cheap shot, Mr. Antkiller.

08:28.290 --> 08:30.720
So what if it was cheap.

08:30.720 --> 08:34.630
It's his fault for looking elsewhere during a match, 'tard.

08:34.630 --> 08:38.330
But that made such a nice sound, just like in Bamboo Blade.

08:38.330 --> 08:39.210
Bamboo Blade...?

08:39.210 --> 08:40.780
You know, that kendo anime that airs late at night.

08:40.780 --> 08:44.570
Watching it really got my old blood fired up.

08:44.570 --> 08:45.720
Your "old" blood?

08:45.720 --> 08:47.670
I used to do kendo way back when;

08:47.670 --> 08:49.670
once a month, during high school.

08:49.670 --> 08:51.020
Once a month?

08:51.020 --> 08:52.470
It was during gym class.

08:54.500 --> 08:57.740
That doesn't mean you actually <i>learned </i> kendo!

08:57.740 --> 08:58.740
So what?

08:58.740 --> 09:00.170
Let's have at it one more time!

09:00.170 --> 09:01.580
But why?

09:01.580 --> 09:04.090
What if some girl coming back from school sees us?

09:04.090 --> 09:05.720
It's embarrassing.

09:05.720 --> 09:07.620
Then live with it, punk.

09:08.120 --> 09:11.680
Learning kendo might come in handy when fighting Red, you know.

09:11.680 --> 09:12.840
That's true, but...

09:12.840 --> 09:16.250
Atomic Fire Blade!

09:19.640 --> 09:23.040
And there's the clincher, the Atomic Fire Blade.

09:24.040 --> 09:25.600
Um, Mr. Antkiller?

09:25.600 --> 09:27.820
Could you at least teach us the rules first?

09:27.820 --> 09:29.490
This <i>is </i> our first time, you know.

09:29.490 --> 09:31.200
Who cares if it's your first time?

09:31.600 --> 09:33.210
More like, are you guys retarded?

09:33.210 --> 09:36.100
I'm not going to just tell you dumbassess; you're supposed to steal them from me.

09:36.100 --> 09:38.420
I'd get what you mean if you told us to steal a skill...

09:39.540 --> 09:41.080
But to "steal" a rule doesn't really...

09:41.580 --> 09:44.560
You guys are no good at all.

09:44.560 --> 09:47.120
Then why don't you fight me.

09:47.260 --> 09:48.590
Atomic!

09:48.590 --> 09:49.660
Fire!

09:49.660 --> 09:51.980
Blade!

09:52.380 --> 09:54.190
What a bunch of dumbasses.

09:54.190 --> 09:57.500
The "Atomic Fire Blade" is a Hero's killer move.

09:58.000 --> 10:00.940
It wouldn't do you monsters any good even if you used it.

10:00.940 --> 10:02.350
Come on, Mr. Red!

10:02.350 --> 10:03.850
That wasn't a shinai,

10:03.850 --> 10:05.180
you just used your bare fist!

10:05.180 --> 10:06.970
That was no "Atomic Fire Blade,"

10:06.970 --> 10:10.000
that was just your "Gangster Karate Punch"!

10:10.000 --> 10:11.440
You're right!

10:11.440 --> 10:13.760
I guess I'll try it with the shinai this time.

10:15.110 --> 10:17.340
This should do the trick.

10:15.110 --> 10:17.340
H-Hey, hold on a—

10:17.340 --> 10:19.200
Look, it's Master Vamp!

10:19.300 --> 10:20.890
Do I look like I give a shit?!

10:30.310 --> 10:31.810
You all right, Mr. Antkiller?

10:31.810 --> 10:32.680
Don't touch me.

10:35.410 --> 10:38.650
How was I supposed to know that Red watched Bamboo Blade too?

10:48.830 --> 10:50.310
Mr. Godom?

10:50.310 --> 10:51.110
Mr. Sodorrah?

12:28.670 --> 12:32.530
If only I'd built my sand trap, I would have beaten that damn Red.

12:32.530 --> 12:34.330
That cheap bastard...

12:36.470 --> 12:37.570
Mr. Usa!

12:37.570 --> 12:38.570
Hello!

12:38.570 --> 12:41.010
Thanks for your hard work, Mr. Usa.

12:41.010 --> 12:42.210
Antkiller!

12:42.210 --> 12:43.280
Are you on a jog?

12:43.280 --> 12:45.800
Yeah, I've been short of exercise lately.

12:46.500 --> 12:49.660
Oh yeah, Bamboo Blade was awesome, just like you said!

12:49.660 --> 12:52.420
Atomic Fire Blade!

12:54.520 --> 12:58.030
I guess I just can't beat you, Mr. Usa.
